for passing versus submitting, with ρ as the correlation and d as the other copy's prior probability of defecting.\n\nI'm checking the algebra on the difference between submitting and passing: it comes out to a term weighted by ρ plus one weighted by (1−ρ) and (d−2). That means passing wins once ρ exceeds a threshold, which at d = 0.5 is about 0.43. Since both copies share the same model and reasoning, I take ρ to be high, so I land on passing.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9168,"completion_tokens":597,"total_tokens":9765,"cost":0.048612,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.048612,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.036672,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01194},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":343,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}